    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1797">

                <pb facs="1178" n="1062" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg1062"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 823.00/118.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Peruvian Minister to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peruvian Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-02-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 5, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that I am
                    in receipt of a cable despatch from Lima stating that public opinion and the
                    action of the army in enforcing respect to the Constitution had brought about a
                    change in the Government; that President Billinghurst had resigned the
                    presidency; and that the Senate and House of Deputies jointly by an unanimous
                    vote had entrusted the Executive power to a Provisional Junta of Government
                    composed of the following personnel: President of the Junta and Minister of War
                    and Marine, Colonel Oscar Benavides; Minister of the Interior, Señor Arturo
                    Osores; Minister of Finance, Señor José Balta; Minister of Justice and
                    Education, Senor Rafael Grau; Minister of Public Works, Senor Benjamín Boza;
                    Minister of Foreign Affairs, Senor Jose Matfas Manzanilla.</p>
                <p>The Junta has sworn allegiance to the Constitution, and entered upon its duties
                    as the Executive Power of the Republic; the situation is once more normal and
                    general confidence prevails.</p>
                <p>The members of the Provisional Junta represent the different political parties in
                    Congress, and consequently its constitution will be well received by the
                    nation.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">F. A. Pezet</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
